# The Dark Knight's fourth job node, and the second swing in the game the
# player HOLDS rather than presses: the spear turns into a dark storm for four
# seconds and the release throws eight shockwaves out of it.
#
# One skill, not two, and the fight decides how long to hold it. A map mob dies
# to the shockwave alone, so the hold is let go at its floor and the cast is
# almost all release; a boss never does, so it is held out to all 26 pulses.
# That is Channel's own rule -- see CombatSim::ChannelPulses -- and it lands
# GMS's mobbing and bossing readings without either being written down.
#
# The 870ms floor is the 150ms wind-up and the 720ms release, which one pulse
# fits inside. Every frame of both is positive, so the floor takes the attack
# speed stage; the 140ms pulse clock is the skill's own, as a held swing's
# always is.
#
# GMS heals 1% of the pool for every one of the 26 attacks and 10% for every
# one of the 120 final attacks -- 1,226% of the pool, which is a full heal and
# is meant to be. Both are stated as GMS states them rather than folded flat,
# so anything that ever cuts healing cuts the right number.
#
# Dropped: the knockback and status immunity while it winds up, and the
# shockwave ignoring attack reflection -- nothing here inflicts either.
name: "Calamitous Cyclone"
description:
  "Swings a spear so fast it creates a dark storm and devastates the area in "
  "front of you."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_DARK_KNIGHT_V skill_order: 3 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_SPEAR
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_POLEARM
base_delay_ms: 870
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
max_enemies: 12
lines: 8
base {
  skill_pct: 2.64
  crit_rate: 1.00
  ied_pct: 0.50
  hp_recover_pct: 0.01
}
per_level { skill_pct: 0.11 }
channel {
  pulse_interval_ms: 140
  max_pulses: 26
  finish_delay_ms: 720
  damage_taken_pct: 0.50
  finish {
    label: "Shockwave"
    lines: 15
    casts: 8
    base {
      skill_pct: 5.87
      hp_recover_pct: 0.10
    }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.23 }
  }
}
